package wk:automergefs;

/// A node that IS a synced filesystem: an Automerge repo in pushwork's vfs
/// shape (a directory doc of path → file-doc urls), kept live over a
/// subduction websocket, served to the nodes it's wired into via
/// `wk:fs/provider`. The subduction server stays wherever it is (a Docker
/// container on the host, reached through a HostService node); this guest is
/// the sync client.
///
/// A command component (`wasi:cli/run` is its main), because it needs
/// wasi:sockets — which the wasip1 adapter world cargo-component targets does
/// not have. Serving and syncing share the one guest thread, so the serve
/// loop uses `poll-request` (bounded wait), never the blocking `next-request`.
world automergefs {
    import wk:fs/provider;
}
